course: dictionary
lesson: 7730
title: Puffy: two meanings in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them tell you which meaning the writer wants. «Her eyes were puffy after she cried.» Eyes that are puffy after crying look swollen, so puffy means swollen here.
explain: «Cumulus are white puffy heaps of fair weather.» Heaps of fair weather are soft and round, so puffy means soft, round and full of air here. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the picture in the sentence?
explain: Check by trying your meaning in the sentence. Swollen fits eyes and ankles, but a cloud cannot be swollen with crying. Soft and full of air fits clouds, jackets and sleeves. If your meaning does not fit, try the other one.
fact: Puffy means swollen, often around the eyes or face, from crying, sleep or an injury.
fact: Puffy also means soft, round and full of air, like a puffy jacket or puffy clouds.
fact: Puffy is an adjective. Its comparison forms are puffier and puffiest.
fact: «Puffy eyes» and «puffy clouds» show the two meanings of the same word.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Her eyes were puffy after she cried.» What does puffy mean here? | Thin and pointed | Bright and shiny | *Swollen | Cold to touch
exercise: «The puffy jacket kept Sam warm all day.» What does puffy mean here? | Wet and cold | Very fast | Swollen and sore | *Soft and full of air
exercise: Oliver says puffy must always mean swollen. What is the best answer? | Yes, puffy only ever means swollen | No, puffy means sad and tired | *No, puffy can also mean soft, round and full of air, as in «puffy clouds» | Yes, puffy is only used for animals
test: «His ankle was puffy after the sprain, so he put ice on it.» Which meaning fits here? | Soft and full of air | *Swollen | Bright red | Fast-moving
test: «Cumulus clouds are white and puffy and usually mean fair weather.» Which meaning fits here? | Swollen from crying | Sharp and cold | *Soft, round and full of air | Dark and stormy
exam: Which sentence uses puffy to mean swollen? | «The puffy sleeves of her dress were blue.» | «The puffy jacket kept him warm.» | «The puffy clouds drifted over the hill.» | *«His nose was puffy after he bumped it on the door.»
